From 7f8e835b14cab0d03686cf77866c10e9f096a7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phrac <derek@disflux.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:13:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Session bridge: mirror local sessions into one Matrix room
 (thread per session)

Desktop/TUI/webui-born sessions never touch Matrix, so FluxChat clients can't
see or steer them. The bridge runs as a gateway watcher: it polls the session
store and mirrors each eligible session into ONE room as a thread (root =
session announcement; user rows and final replies as thread replies; working
bubble settled via org.fluxchat.agent edits, reusing patch-0002/0004 protocol
semantics so clients need zero changes).

Room identity is the org.hermes.sessions state event (version 1 + sources),
never the title; the bridge sets the marker itself when it creates the room.
Matrix-origin and internal sessions are excluded; draft sessions get no thread
until their first user row. Cost rides org.fluxchat.agent.cost_usd only when
integral (Tuwunel canonical JSON rejects floats; FluxChat serde rejects
strings); sub-dollar costs fold into the result headline.

Inbound: thread replies from controller accounts (session_bridge_controllers)
resume the mapped session via a headless turn; mirror-sent events are output
and never echo back as input. The Matrix adapter drops foreign events for the
bridge room via is_bridge_room so gateway session machinery never answers
there. Config: matrix.extra.session_bridge{,_room,_sources,_invite,
_controllers,_backfill_days}.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_session_bridge.py (17).
